🔥 THIS is how most first bugs are found
🧠 2. MENTAL MODELS (THIS IS THE REAL SECRET)

Forget tools for a second. This is how pros think:

🧩 Model 1: “Trust Boundaries”

Ask:

“What is the server trusting that it shouldn’t?”

Examples:

User ID from request
Role from frontend
Hidden fields

👉 Break that trust

🔄 Model 2: “What if I change this?”

Every parameter:

ID → change it
Role → escalate it
Price → reduce it

👉 Simple but powerful

🚪 Model 3: “Can I go where I shouldn’t?”

Try:

/admin
/api/admin
Other users’ data
🔍 Model 4: “Where does my input go?”

Trace:

Input → server → response

Ask:

Is it reflected? (XSS)
Is it stored? (Stored XSS)
🧠 Model 5: “Developer Assumptions”

Developers assume:

Users behave normally
IDs won’t be changed
Requests won’t be replayed

👉 Your job = break assumptions

